Um, so, uh, IPv6 to me is close to 96 times larger.

00:27:37.005 --> 00:27:38.275
Um, this is actually a

00:27:38.275 --> 00:27:41.900
very interesting academic research question to me is how do you scan IPv6?

00:27:41.900 --> 00:27:44.090
How do you understand these devices?

00:27:44.090 --> 00:27:46.505
It's not possible to just brute force.

00:27:46.505 --> 00:27:52.470
That's not going to work. Um, you have to have a much more intelligent kind of plan,

00:27:52.470 --> 00:27:54.990
uh, a more al- algorithmic approach where you look at

00:27:54.990 --> 00:27:57.140
[NOISE] what devices have been deployed.

00:27:57.140 --> 00:28:02.090
Can you detect what addressing schemes have been used in different regions?

